invariant: INV-7
file: webpki_cfg.c
catches: webpki_session_aes
builds: bin/webpki_session_aes
reason: ch_connect takes a ch_cfg.cipher_suites list that names a code
  point the build does not hold, here TLS_AES_128_CCM_SHA256, and the hello
  offers a suite this client holds no cipher for. A server that selects it
  then meets a refusal a configuration check should have made before a
  byte left (webpki_cfg.h).

--- old
        if (suite_hash_len(cfg->cipher_suites[i]) == 0 || suite_repeats(cfg, i)) {
--- new
        if (suite_repeats(cfg, i)) {
